 structures appear intact.','No radiographic evidence of acute intra-abdominal pathology.','',5,7,'2026-08-26 14:07:11','Abdomen (Pedia)','inactive','1970-01-01 00:00:00',52,'2026-08-26 14:00:27',0,NULL),(325,'GAP2026-00262',117,1,'X-Ray','Apicolordotic View','Routine','Without PhilHealth Card',NULL,'Completed','Pending','Uploaded','[\"public\\/assets\\/uploads\\/cases\\/case_325_1787728700_0.png\"]',1,'2026-08-26 07:18:01','','The lung fields are clear without evidence of focal consolidation, mass, or infiltrates. The cardiac silhouette is within normal limits in size and configuration. The costophrenic angles are sharp and well-defined. No pleural effusion or pneumothorax is seen. The visualized osseous structures are intact.\n','No radiographic evidence of active cardiopulmonary disease.\n','',5,7,'2026-08-26 15:55:01','Apicolordotic View','inactive','1970-01-01 00:00:00',59,'2026-08-26 15:18:20',0,NULL);
